WEBVTT

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:04.690
I see...

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:07.190
Koro Sensei, was it?

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:09.780
The Big Bad teaching students
how to kill the Big Bad...

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:14.240
Pope Gakuho Asano:

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:16.320
having defeated many Big Bads in his time,

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:20.290
was our national hero
and trainer of new heroes in turn.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.750
And? What is this Big Bad doing now?

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:27.710
--Those kids of mine are on
a serious egg-eating kick these days.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:27.710
--He appears to be in line to purchase eggs.

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:31.300
--I'll have to really stock up today,
that's for sure!

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:31.300
--Are you pulling my leg?

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:47.440
"Koro Sensei Quest"

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:56.860
"Nagisa"

00:00:57.990 --> 00:00:58.530
"Karma"

00:00:59.160 --> 00:00:59.530
"Kaede"

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:00.870
"Isogai" "Maehara"

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:03.540
"Rio" "Okuda" "Sugino" "Kanzaki"

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.040
"Chiba" "Hayami"

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:06.540
"Hinata" "Meg"

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.040
"Hinano" "Takebayashi" "Toka" "Justice"

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:11.050
"Muramatsu" "Kirara" "Yoshida" "Terasaka"

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:13.050
"Okajima" "Hara" "Mimura" "Fuwa" "Sugaya"

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.050
"Karasuma" "Irina"

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:31.360
"The Ruins of Tribulation"

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:35.690
I find it rather difficult to believe
that <i>that</i> is the Big Bad.

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:39.070
Do you truly know what a Big Bad is?

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:39.950
"The Complete Big Bad"

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:40.200
Of course!

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:42.660
"Piercing eyes with a scorching glare."

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:49.420
"<i>The Complete Big Bad</i>, chapter 2"

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:45.250
"A jaw that could pulverize a dragon's head."

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:47.210
"Claws that can tear through steel."

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:49.710
"Heels that gouge the earth."

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:53.250
He's 0 for 4!

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:55.090
Are you pulling my leg?

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:57.170
I understand how you must feel,
but it's the truth!

00:01:57.470 --> 00:01:59.220
All right, then.

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:03.890
However, I doubt the Big Bad
has the aptitude to be an instructor.

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:05.850
What shall we do?

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:09.810
Let us give him a little test.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:16.070
Careful, everyone. It's really dark.

00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:17.030
Ow!

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:18.240
And narrow, too.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.700
Hey! Someone touched my behind!

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:22.110
Okajima!

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:23.520
It wasn't me!

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:28.020
Oh? Is that the way out?

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:36.260
"1st Chamber"

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:36.260
All right, class--here's today's destination:
the Ruins of Tribulation.

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:39.800
I've never come this far on a quest before!

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:41.050
It's so exciting!

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:43.780
Is this what it means to be
a journeying party of heroes?

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:45.220
Hey! You there!

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:48.230
Enough getting carried away--
follow my example!

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:50.440
<i>Who's</i> getting carried away?!

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:52.560
--Listen, you've got way too many items!

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:52.560
--If the Pope is giving us
a dungeon-clearing quest,

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:54.480
--They're so crammed in, that mirror 
broke--and it looks like a key item!

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:54.480
--If the Pope is giving us 
a dungeon-clearing quest,

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.860
--They're so crammed in,
that mirror broke--and it looks like a key item!

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.860
--I have to think he's 
got an ulterior motive.

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:58.780
--I've got to fix that!

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:00.450
--Here, let me get right on it.

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:00.450
--A trial, right? That's like a pop quiz.

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:02.410
Right, Koro Sensei?

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:05.860
Clear this and I get a raise...
Clear this and I get a raise...

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:07.580
--He's not listening.
--Ah, yes, everything will be fine.

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:09.870
Who knew the Big Bad got a salary?

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:11.830
I wonder who's fastest at handing out raises?

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:15.750
Hi, gang! I'm the guardian 
of these here ruins.

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:16.800
Nice to meet you!

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:19.670
And here come the trials!

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:23.340
Breeze on through them
so we can report to the pope!

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:25.850
Oh, my my my! "Breeze on through"?

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:27.770
Maybe I misheard you.

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:33.100
Shaddap! Always a pleasure to see you
full-of-yourself bottom-feeders!

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:37.810
You're nothing but useless
trash garbage taking these trials!

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:40.940
What's his deal?

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:44.410
There are three chambers of tribulation!
Here is your first trial!

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:46.160
Huh? What?

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:49.910
Surely even garbage ninnymuggins
can <i>read</i>, can't they?

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:52.120
Wh-What a pain...

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:56.130
What's this? "The first chamber
is the Chamber of Impostors."

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:59.590
"We've slipped an impostor into your party."

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:01.720
An impostor? When did this happen?

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:03.340
Along that dark path earlier!

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:07.680
"The first trial is to find the impostor
and remove them from your party."

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.770
So we have to suspect our friends?

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:13.480
I'm the real thing! Don't kick me out, okay?

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:16.440
Please believe me! <i>I</i> am the <i>real thing</i>!

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:16.440
"The Big Bad is panicking!"

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:19.530
You believe me, don't you, Nagisa?!

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:21.650
The teacher doth protest too much, methinks.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:21.650
"The Big Bad is panicking badly!"

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:24.280
Just look at these cute round eyes!

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:27.490
How could I be a monster
with such unclouded eyes?

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:29.620
You're the Big Bad--
that's what makes you a monster.

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:32.540
--But I'll get fewer parts
if I'm not in the party!

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:34.750
--He can't pass this trial unless 
he knows his students well.

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:33.540
--What do you mean, "parts"?

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:35.960
--Chances to shine!

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:40.800
First of all, one cannot expect
a Big Bad to lend an ear to any human.

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:44.260
He'll likely start by kicking out
the ones who defy him.

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:48.850
Now show us... the true 
nature of the Big Bad.

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:50.810
"Ruins of Tribulation: Chamber 1's Trial"
"Who Is the Impostor!?"

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:50.810
Okay, anyone else have any thoughts?

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:52.350
He's lending his ear!

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:56.770
What do we do? I haven't the foggiest idea.

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:58.150
This is a tough one.

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:00.020
Who's the impostor?

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:01.100
Believe!

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:04.150
--Sir!
--Yes, Okajima?

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:08.370
If they'd just let me smell them,
I could totally sniff out the real girls!

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:12.290
It seems Okajima is the real deal.

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:16.080
I think we should kick 
Okajima out either way!

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:19.210
I just found a way to spot the fake.

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:22.210
Even if they can fake
Koro Sensei's appearance,

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:25.170
they can't duplicate his 
speed and such. Right?

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:27.180
Oh, I get it!

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:28.510
That's our Karma!

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:32.350
As a hurdle to overcome,
this trial really wasn't all that.

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:32.890
"Karma's luck decreases!"

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:37.560
Whoa! But he's real!

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:41.020
"Karma left the party!"

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:38.520
What awful luck!

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:41.020
Yeah, Karma's probably fine.

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:46.240
"Tell Us, Mr. Principal!"

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:45.070
Tell Us, Mr. Principal!

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:51.030
Hello, students. Principal Gakuho Asano here.

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:56.040
Seems we have a lot of questions
from distressed students again today.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:58.540
Now, let's try to address their concerns.

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:02.960
Here's one from "Class Pet Duty":

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:06.170
"I'm infatuated with this older man.

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:09.430
How do I go about catching his eye?"

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:10.430
Hmm.

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:12.600
Romantic advice, is it?

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:15.370
First you must take
complete control of this man.

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:17.810
It's really quite simple:

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:20.310
His hobbies, address, family structure,

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:23.980
his parents' salaries,
household income, and savings...

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:26.650
Secure all the information you can obtain.

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:29.280
The more weaknesses for you to latch on to,

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:32.160
the easier it is to control a person.

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:36.140
Begin by controlling a classmate,
bending them to your will.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:39.080
If you're incapable of even that much,

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:41.670
consider yourself ineligible for roma--

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:43.340
Koro-Q!

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:43.670
"Koro Sensei Quest"

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:45.710
So <i>this</i> is the impostor.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:47.760
That's one pretty Terasaka.

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:48.760
Good job!

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:52.470
So you saw through him.
Not bad for trash garbage.

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:54.390
But the real thing is safe and sound, right?

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:56.850
Why can't <i>this</i> be the real thing?

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:59.310
"2nd Chamber"

00:06:57.140 --> 00:06:59.310
All right, losers: onto the next trial!

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:01.690
"The second chamber
is the Chamber of Secrets."

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:06.150
--"Tell the guardian a party member's
secret that only you know."

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:06.150
--What kind of trial is <i>that</i>?

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:07.780
A party member's secret...

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:09.240
That's one brutal trial.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:11.490
This happens to be my specialty!

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:17.200
"Notebook of Students' Secrets - Top Secret"

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:17.200
Getting a handle on students'
daily lifestyles is part of a teacher's job!

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:19.660
"Abs & thighs (and self-delusion)"

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:19.660
While I snooped in on 
all sorts of situations,

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:22.370
I built up a collection
of all your most massive secrets!

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:22.120
"Solo air guitar in the woods at night"

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:24.590
--Sugi-Strike!
--What a lowlife!

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:24.590
"Sugi-Strike!"
"Practicing special moves"

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:27.880
An instructor must know all
of his students' secrets and weaknesses

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:30.170
if he is to control them.

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:32.510
Not bad at all.

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:34.640
Which one of you is the Big Bad again?

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:38.100
"Notebook of Students' Secrets - Top Secret"

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:36.640
That's awful, sir!

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:38.100
If that's how you want to be...

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:40.810
"Notebook of Koro Sensei's Secrets"

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:40.810
A notebook of <i>my</i> secrets?!

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:44.770
--Stop that! I'll listen to anything you say!

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:46.020
--What? Seriously?
--Stop that! I'll listen to anything you say!

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:50.440
"The Pope is stunned!"

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:50.440
<i>They</i> have <i>him</i> figured out!

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:53.660
Mortifying! Oh, so mortifying!
So, so mortifying!

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:54.700
"3rd Chamber"

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:59.790
For your final trial, I've prepared
something right up you losers' alley!

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:05.250
The last trial is in
the Chamber of Self-Sacrifice.

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:06.290
The ceiling!

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:10.380
In only a few minutes,
the ceiling will have dropped completely!

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:13.970
Unfortunately, this is where
your trial comes in.

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:15.760
It's simple enough:

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:18.470
Press the button and the door
on the opposite side will open.

00:08:18.850 --> 00:08:20.560
But the second it's pressed,

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:24.190
the door on <i>that</i> side
can never be opened again.

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:27.940
If we press our button,
only our teacher will be saved.

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:31.900
Conversely, unless he presses
<i>his</i> button, we'll die.

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:33.280
What the hell?!

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:39.580
Can he kill himself to save his students?

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:41.950
This trial reveals the 
instructor's very nature.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:45.540
A monster has no business
working as a teacher.

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:49.750
Come, Big Bad: here's where
you reveal your hideous character!

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:50.460
Boop!

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:54.380
"The Pope is confused!"

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:57.590
Abandonment is not an option.

00:08:57.590 --> 00:08:59.350
After all, they're my students.

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:02.850
--Koro Sensei! Oh, sir!
--Let's go rescue him!
--Hang tight!

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:05.350
So this is the E Class teacher...

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:08.520
How... how exquisite...!

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:11.650
Love.

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:17.450
Koro-Q!

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:18.120
"Koro Sensei Quest"

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:21.290
That will be all for today.

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:21.950
So then...

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:25.960
I shall recognize him as a teacher
at Kunugigaoka Magic Academy.

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:27.250
However...

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:30.170
I will cut him loose at any time
if I judge him unnecessary

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:32.640
to my educational vision.

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:35.260
Even if he <i>is</i> the Big Bad.

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:39.300
Okay, we've completed
the quest--let's head back.

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:40.180
Yes, sir!

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:42.010
You know...

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:44.560
If we'd left him locked
in that room in the last trial,

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:47.560
we could've beaten Koro Sensei, no sweat.

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:48.400
Oh.

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:50.520
You guys are too soft.

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:53.980
What awful luck!

00:09:53.980 --> 00:09:57.240
And <i>that's</i> what we call
"taking a fall for a gag," class!

00:09:57.240 --> 00:09:58.660
Yes, sir!
